  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    counts = {}\n    for row in grid:\n        for val in row:\n            if val != 0:\n                counts[val] = counts.get(val, 0) + 1\n                \n    # Sort the non-zero elements by their frequency in descending order\n    sorted_counts = sorted(counts.items(), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n    \n    # The most frequent non-zero element is the background/filler for the blocks\n    # The remaining elements are the target shapes\n    target_elements = sorted_counts[1:]\n    \n    # Create the output grid as a single column of the remaining elements\n    output = [[val] for val, count in target_elements]\n    \n    return output\n```",
